  "verbalization": "Excisusin B is shown to have multiple targets, including Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase, sodium/bile acid cotransporter, and multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, all of which are implicated in the regulation of Tyrosine--tRNA ligase. The evidence suggests that Excisusin B may act as a modulator of the expression or activity of these proteins, which in turn influence the function of Tyrosine--tRNA ligase. The scores from the different paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship between Excisusin B and Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, with varying degrees of support from different molecular targets. The integration of these findings implies that Excisusin B could potentially regulate Tyrosine--tRNA ligase through a network of interconnected proteins, possibly by affecting their expression or activity. The mechanism underlying this relationship remains to be fully elucidated, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction between Excisusin B and Tyrosine--tRNA ligase.",
